# A DHCPOFFER as dnsmasq 2.91 sent it: one Ethernet frame, 342 bytes,
# exactly as captured.
#
# Observed on 2026-11-21 at Unix time 1795245120.949489, on the bridge
# br-n1 of the Linux-bridge lab -- dnsmasq 2.91 on Debian 13, kernel
# 6.12.117+deb13-amd64, serving dhcp-range=10.0.0.100,10.0.0.150,12h on
# the gateway interface gw-n1. This answers request.hex. case.toml
# beside this file carries the capture's full provenance and the
# docs/provenance.md rows the pair supports.
#
# These are bytes observed coming out of a running program. Nothing here
# is derived from dnsmasq's source code, and nothing may be: dnsmasq is
# GPL-2/3 and teneral is Apache-2.0, so an observation is the only
# lawful source for a behaviour no RFC specifies.
#
# Hex text rather than a binary blob, for two reasons: a reviewer can
# read the diff when a fixture changes, and the bytes can carry the
# field annotations below. The harness strips comments and whitespace
# and compares what decodes. The annotations are a reading aid; the
# bytes are what the rig asserts on.

# Ethernet: dst fa:16:3e:00:01:0a, src fa:16:3e:00:01:01, type 0x0800 (IPv4)
fa 16 3e 00 01 0a fa 16 3e 00 01 01 08 00

# IPv4: 10.0.0.1 -> 10.0.0.128, protocol 17, total length 328
45 c0 01 48 40 5a 00 00 40 11 24 0b 0a 00 00 01
0a 00 00 80

# UDP: 67 -> 68, length 308, checksum 0x15c6
00 43 00 44 01 34 15 c6

# BOOTP: op=2 htype=1 hlen=6 hops=0
02 01 06 00
# xid=0x2c72847d, secs=0, flags=0x0000 (broadcast flag clear)
2c 72 84 7d 00 00 00 00
# ciaddr=0.0.0.0 yiaddr=10.0.0.128 siaddr=10.0.0.1 giaddr=0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00 0a 00 00 80 0a 00 00 01 00 00 00 00
# chaddr=fa:16:3e:00:01:0a, padded to 16 bytes
fa 16 3e 00 01 0a 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
# sname, 64 bytes, unused
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
# file, 128 bytes, unused
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
# magic cookie 99.130.83.99
63 82 53 63

# Options, one per line, in the order they were sent.
35 01 02                                        # option 53 dhcp-message-type: OFFER (2)
36 04 0a 00 00 01                               # option 54 server-identifier: 10.0.0.1
33 04 00 00 a8 c0                               # option 51 ip-address-lease-time: 43200 seconds
3a 04 00 00 54 60                               # option 58 renewal-time-t1: 21600 seconds
3b 04 00 00 93 a8                               # option 59 rebinding-time-t2: 37800 seconds
01 04 ff ff ff 00                               # option 1 subnet-mask: 255.255.255.0
1c 04 0a 00 00 ff                               # option 28 broadcast-address: 10.0.0.255
03 04 0a 00 00 01                               # option 3 router: 10.0.0.1
06 04 0a 00 00 01                               # option 6 domain-name-server: 10.0.0.1
ff                                              # option 255 end

# 8 bytes of padding after the end option.
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
